## SEVERITY FLOOR (so you do not argue it later)
- `credentialShapes` or any other export of `secrets.ts` differing from main's on ANY input in your corpus, or any product (non-test) caller of `renderedTextCredentialShapes`, or any input path, record check or `checked()` guard moved to the variant = **Blocker**.
- A real credential (an input on which main's strict function returns `config_directive`, that is not itself a pure label run) that the rendered-text scan does not report = **Major** if the variant has a product caller, otherwise **Minor** (it weakens a test oracle only) unless Tuesday's stamp ruling 3 says otherwise. A rendered-text scan that stops reporting a rule other than `config_directive` = **Blocker**. The cost the builder disclosed (a typed title-cased line with a camel-case letters-only value, e.g. `Username Admin Password HunterTwo`, is skipped in rendered text only) = **Note for Kam**, not a finding.
- A removed item, control, field or source id; an old key changed or dropped; the five old `sources` hashes moved; a bundle `CONTENT_HASH` that does not equal the repo's own recompute = **Blocker**. A new field with a value, target, default, severity or remediation = **Blocker** (lane L2's, K3).
- Any Q-03/Q-04 pattern hit on the committed sources, the bundles' added rows or the PR's added lines = **Blocker**; a string in the derived sources that is neither an id nor a name present in the upstream catalogue or the names-only file = **Blocker**; a derived file not reproducible by its CLI from the upstream bytes = **Blocker**; the importer failing to refuse an id not in the source = **Blocker**.
- A client or sample-client name, or a decision-card id (it carries the client abbreviation), in an added line, a commit message, a file name, the PR title or body = **Major** (B341-1 precedent). **A person's first name (the client's contact) in a commit message only, the squash message and body being Tuesday's to write = Minor,** unless Tuesday's stamp ruling 1 says Major; in an added line or a file name = Major.
- The register page: any row that breaks inside a lower-case run at a place the renderer does not break by design (your own detector, r5), a cell clipped or overlapping its neighbour, a table edge past the right margin, or a header word that does not fit its column = **Major**; a policy PDF without exceptions, or any other PDF, moving in bytes with no nameable camel-case or "(" token as the cause = **Blocker** (the builder claims only those move); a DOCX whose TEXT (not column widths) differs from the same code with the register weights at base = **Blocker**; the smaller 7.2 pt text, the look of the register, the wider/narrower DOCX columns = **Note for Kam** (looks are Kam's, K7).
- The printed contents numbers of the policy PDF (B323's lane) no longer equalling the rendered pages on the 137-item real release = **Blocker** (the earlier gates measured 55 items).
- A rendered artefact carrying a builder-written provenance or citation sentence (STATUS `:108`) that reaches a customer = **Minor** (a NEW WORD for Kam's words card, K9, nothing ships); a new Datasec-authored word in `packages/renderers/src` string literals = **Minor**.
- An existing test weakened (an `expect(` removed, a bound loosened, a full-list comparison turned into a subset or a count, a title retitled to hide a lost check) = **Blocker**; a `.skip` / `.only` / `.todo` / `retry` / `skipIf` / `test.fails` / `expect.soft` added = **Blocker**; a test name present at base and absent at head with no nameable reason = **Blocker**; a regression (green at base, red at head, with a control that it is not load) = **Blocker**. The mutant table: a surviving mutant on the strict/rendered split (S1-S4), the importer refusal (I1-I3) or the register fit (R1-R4) with no equivalence argument = **Major**; on any other row = **Minor** unless your probe shows the reachable wrong answer (then **Major**).
- Anything cut, merged, migrated, registered or deployed; `main` moved by this branch; a ref deleted by the gate = **Blocker**.
